Sorry, but it's not really clear.<br><br>AO-123 is already part of the satellites list.<br>But as a general safety usage, it would be better for you to keep your modified satellites.txt file in your Documents folder, and copy it to the OpenGD77 CPS installation folder after a software update. This way you can't lose your modifications.<br>BTW, as it already happened, double check the pristine satellites.txt file before dropping your modified version, as data structure can evolve.<br><br>The other trick (with the same content checking mentionned above) is to select a non-standard satellites.txt file. For this, in the "OpenGD77 support" window, hold down the Control key before clicking the "Install satellite keps" button. A file picker will appear, select your satellites.txt file (e.g located in your Documents folder).<br>The selected file will be stored as the default satellites.txt file, until it gets invalid or missing.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=56">F1RMB</a> — Sat Feb 15, 2025 3:42 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
